<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" data-theme={assigns[:theme]} class="scroll-smooth">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex" />
    <title>Slow down · Confluence Mirror</title>
    <link phx-track-static rel="stylesheet" href={~p"/assets/css/app.css"} />
    <style :if={assigns[:skin_css] not in [nil, ""]}>
      <%= Phoenix.HTML.raw(assigns[:skin_css]) %>
    </style>
  </head>
  <body class="flex min-h-screen items-center justify-center bg-base-100 px-4 text-base-content antialiased">
    <main class="w-full max-w-lg rounded-2xl border border-base-300/70 bg-base-100 p-8 text-center shadow-sm">
      <p class="text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-primary">429</p>
      <h1 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-semibold leading-tight">Too many requests</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-base-content/70">
        This mirror limits how often one reader may load pages, so one busy script cannot slow it down for everyone.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm font-medium">
        Try again in {assigns[:retry_after] || 60} seconds.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-2">
        <a href={~p"/"} class="btn btn-primary btn-sm">Home</a>
        <a href={~p"/search"} class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm">Search</a>
        <a href={~p"/spaces"} class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm">All spaces</a>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-6 text-[11px] text-base-content/70">
        Automation should use the JSON API, which answers with a <code>Retry-After</code> header.
      </p>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
